node_modules/

# `.maestro/` is machine state — worktrees, cached session ids, the deployed server binary — with
# one exception: `profiles.json` says what a reviewer *is* for this project, which is a property of
# the project rather than of the machine, so it is committed. The directory has to be excluded
# entry by entry rather than wholesale, because git will not descend into an ignored directory to
# find a negated pattern inside it.
.maestro/*
!.maestro/profiles.json
